  "implementation": {
    "slabs": "One slab1..272 rows. Helper emits256 when remaining>272, otherwise absorbs final tail;273 rows use256+17. Caller partitions the full chunk and uses actual per-slab query positions.",
    "union": "Union retained canonical I8 drop-mask blocks across slab rows; exclusive local256-block scans, one1024-thread global scan, ordered logical entry IDs and contiguous/paged F16 gathers. Empty extra block and partial final block handled exactly. Eight warps gather eight logical blocks per CTA.",
    "memory": "Source mask has <=2048 retained8-entry blocks per row. Capacity=min(logical keys,rows*16384). Decode at1048576 logical keys reserves16384 gathered rows (4MiB), plus IDs/count/score/scan/top-k workspace. Caller supplies all exact disjoint request-owned buffers. Immutable model and backend weight ownership unchanged.",
    "device_count": "Private GPU-produced bounded I32 count feeds scoring and selection; no host count read or intermediate completion fence. Scorer skips inactive tiles and preserves inactive output tails. Dynamic top-k clamps k to min(512,active_count) in both selection and merge. Public static scoring and top-k plans remain unchanged; separate template variants retain static execution.",
    "positions": "Queries already have actual-position RoPE. Score causality is disabled using capacity*rate, then per-row drop and actual-position logical-entry bounds mask the compact score prefix. Final index list maps compact indices back to logical pool IDs, retaining -1 padding.",
    "contract": "Finite F16 queries/head weights/keys; canonical binary drop mask with at most2048 retained blocks per row. Static logical key count16385..1048576, rate1..256, paged entries128/256 or contiguous. Device count is produced internally. Bounds guards prevent out-of-capacity gathers; masks violating the source cardinality contract are not admitted inputs.",
    "preflight": "All scalar dimensions, exact view counts/types, alignment, request identity, canonical empty unused scratch and pairwise overlap checked before any stage writes. CUDA execution failure marks request failed. No allocation, host transfer, synchronization, source cursors or model position commit inside callback."
  },
